{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019BJxCoMDzRN3WszVNpqSgf","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"b4b76423feb220db7e78f27e769f3d32ffaf89b7\",\"date\":\"2026-09-28T16:06:21+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5916: Reuse generated identifiers when retrying a patient save (#2780)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"dab9f79eef9f57aeee91bd237c0d6431cd9c4f43\",\"date\":\"2026-09-10T20:50:28+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Tell the user when the refine filters, not the query, emptied the search results (#2725)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Tell the user when the refine filters, not the query, emptied the search results\\n\\nWhen a refine filter matched nothing, the results area showed the same message as a query with no hits, \\\"Sorry, no patient charts were found\\\" with a hint to retry with the patient's ID. That points the user at the wrong fix. When the query found patients and the filters removed all of them, the empty state now reads \\\"No patients match these filters\\\" with a hint to remove or change a filter, following the filter empty states in the queues, active visits, patient lists and ward apps. A query that itself found nothing keeps the original message.\\n\\n* Keep loading until every page has landed before blaming the filters\\n\\nThe filters run over the rows loaded so far, and a broad search arrives in waves. After page 1 lands, isLoading is false while later pages are still in flight, so a filter that only matches a later page showed \\\"No patients match these filters\\\" until that page arrived. The results now stay in the loading state while the filtered set is empty and pages are still arriving, and the message appears only once loading has settled. Between waves isValidating drops for a render before the next wave is requested, so the check also compares the pages needed with the pages requested.\\n\\n* docs: clarify translated empty-state props\\n\\nDocument that the empty-state title and hint expect already translated strings, and describe their default messages.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1035f45ff4a778664d6d629a7679fc43046877a1\",\"date\":\"2025-09-09T17:10:56+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5014: Surface actual error messages from appointment status change API (#1963)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Previously, when users attempted to cancel missed appointments, generic error messages were displayed instead of the specific backend validation errors. Now the actual API exception message is properly extracted and shown to users.\\n\\n- Extract error messages from responseBody.error.message chain\\n- Remove square brackets from backend error formatting\\n- Surface specific validation errors like \\\"Appointment status can not be changed from Missed to Cancelled\\\"\\n- Fix SWR cache invalidation issues causing premature UI updates\\n- Enable retry capability by resetting loading state in error handler\\n- Modernize error handling with async/await pattern\\n\\nFixes issue where backend validation errors (e.g., missed appointments cannot be cancelled due to status sequence rules) were not properly communicated to users.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3f2210ba0e6086580e99efdceb0c0aec57a1f1db\",\"date\":\"2023-03-18T07:45:48+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-1974: Remove the retry count for E2E tests (#607)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Randila Premarathne\",\"authorEmail\":\"106733522+RandilaP@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"8dad69237718eee9033487b029b6bcf40a6cb8c2\",\"date\":\"2023-02-27T14:46:31+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-1902: Reduce retry count for failing E2E tests (#564)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Randila Premarathne\",\"authorEmail\":\"106733522+RandilaP@users.noreply.github.com\"}],\"totalCount\":5}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"914fbd69-f2e6-4c63-850b-ad78951c277d","uuid":"4399f830-eaf5-4cd8-aa37-d401ae17bf3f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:49:25.438Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"b4b76423feb220db7e78f27e769f3d32ffaf89b7\",\"date\":\"2026-09-28T16:06:21+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5916: Reuse generated identifiers when retrying a patient save (#2780)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"dab9f79eef9f57aeee91bd237c0d6431cd9c4f43\",\"date\":\"2026-09-10T20:50:28+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Tell the user when the refine filters, not the query, emptied the search results (#2725)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Tell the user when the refine filters, not the query, emptied the search results\\n\\nWhen a refine filter matched nothing, the results area showed the same message as a query with no hits, \\\"Sorry, no patient charts were found\\\" with a hint to retry with the patient's ID. That points the user at the wrong fix. When the query found patients and the filters removed all of them, the empty state now reads \\\"No patients match these filters\\\" with a hint to remove or change a filter, following the filter empty states in the queues, active visits, patient lists and ward apps. A query that itself found nothing keeps the original message.\\n\\n* Keep loading until every page has landed before blaming the filters\\n\\nThe filters run over the rows loaded so far, and a broad search arrives in waves. After page 1 lands, isLoading is false while later pages are still in flight, so a filter that only matches a later page showed \\\"No patients match these filters\\\" until that page arrived. The results now stay in the loading state while the filtered set is empty and pages are still arriving, and the message appears only once loading has settled. Between waves isValidating drops for a render before the next wave is requested, so the check also compares the pages needed with the pages requested.\\n\\n* docs: clarify translated empty-state props\\n\\nDocument that the empty-state title and hint expect already translated strings, and describe their default messages.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1035f45ff4a778664d6d629a7679fc43046877a1\",\"date\":\"2025-09-09T17:10:56+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5014: Surface actual error messages from appointment status change API (#1963)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Previously, when users attempted to cancel missed appointments, generic error messages were displayed instead of the specific backend validation errors. Now the actual API exception message is properly extracted and shown to users.\\n\\n- Extract error messages from responseBody.error.message chain\\n- Remove square brackets from backend error formatting\\n- Surface specific validation errors like \\\"Appointment status can not be changed from Missed to Cancelled\\\"\\n- Fix SWR cache invalidation issues causing premature UI updates\\n- Enable retry capability by resetting loading state in error handler\\n- Modernize error handling with async/await pattern\\n\\nFixes issue where backend validation errors (e.g., missed appointments cannot be cancelled due to status sequence rules) were not properly communicated to users.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3f2210ba0e6086580e99efdceb0c0aec57a1f1db\",\"date\":\"2023-03-18T07:45:48+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-1974: Remove the retry count for E2E tests (#607)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Randila Premarathne\",\"authorEmail\":\"106733522+RandilaP@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"8dad69237718eee9033487b029b6bcf40a6cb8c2\",\"date\":\"2023-02-27T14:46:31+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-1902: Reduce retry count for failing E2E tests (#564)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Randila Premarathne\"