{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgHmzsaueyWtTEGWkXGoy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The form manager now keeps generated identifiers because a retried save used to request a new identifier from the source each time. Commit `b4b76423` (PR #2780, ticket O3-5916) fixed this. The registration form lives in `openmrs-esm-patient-management` under `packages/esm-patient-registration-app`; there is no separate `openmrs-esm-patient-registration-app` repository in Falkon.\n\n**What changed and why**\n\n- **Generated values are reused.** Before the fix, `savePatient` called `generateIdentifier(selectedSource.uuid)` on every attempt. A retry after a failed save therefore consumed another identifier from the source and sent a different value. The fix stores each generated value on a `SavePatientTransactionManager`, keyed by field name and source UUID, and reuses it when the source matches. A new value is generated only when the source changed. (`openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/form-manager.ts:217-235`, `.../form-manager.ts:425-440`)\n- **Completed additions are not repeated.** For an existing patient, the identifier-addition step ran again on retry, so an identifier that had already been added could be added twice. The fix records each successful addition in `addedIdentifiers` and skips it on a later attempt. (`.../form-manager.ts:250-256`)\n- **Tests cover the cases.** The new tests check that a retried new-patient save reuses `10001V`, that a successful addition is not repeated after a later save failure, that a failed addition is retried with the same value, and that a changed source generates a new value. (`.../form-manager.test.ts:724-787`, `.../patient-registration.test.tsx:697`)\n\n**Commit and ticket:** `b4b76423` is \"(fix) O3-5916: Reuse generated identifiers when retrying a patient save (#2780)\". I read the diff of `form-manager.ts` for that commit, and it contains the generation-reuse and addition-skip logic described above. The commit message names ticket O3-5916 and PR #2780.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/form-manager.ts\", \"startLine\": 217, \"endLine\": 235},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/form-manager.ts\", \"startLine\": 250, \"endLine\": 256},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/form-manager.ts\", \"startLine\": 425, \"endLine\": 440},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/form-manager.test.ts\", \"startLine\": 724, \"endLine\": 769},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/form-manager.test.ts\", \"startLine\": 771, \"endLine\": 787},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/patient-registration.test.tsx\", \"startLine\": 697, \"endLine\": 697},\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-management\", \"commit\": \"b4b76423feb220db7e78f27e769f3d32ffaf89b7\"},\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-management\", \"pr\": 2780},\n  {\"ticket\": \"O3-5916\"}\n]\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2105,"cache_read_input_tokens":26503,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2105},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"914fbd69-f2e6-4c63-850b-ad78951c277d","uuid":"0968835c-267e-4212-a835-c2aa46fbb8ad","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:49:37.417Z","request_